 decision/hooks-fail-open · Hooks fail open — Every hook failure fails open: exit 0 with no body.
+decision/input-box-readiness-from-literals · Input box readiness read from compiled literals — The input box reads up only on compiled literals, a footer literal or a rule row of at least 40 rule chars directly above a row opening the prompt char, and never while a modal literal stands; one predicate decides for verify and for viola run's pre-send gate. · why: A boundary widening that was ratified.
 decision/invalid-hook-frames-dropped · Invalid hook frames dropped — An invalid hook.dialog frame is not registered and an invalid hook.event frame is not appended.
@@ -384,3 +385,3 @@
 decision/scratch-footer-reading-residual · Scratch footer reading is no standing permission — A scratch footer reading of a newer CLI is one tmpfs-home run start, no key typed, only scrubbed footer rows kept; it is no product path, and another such reading needs its own answer. · why: accepted residual
-decision/screen-fixture-signature-rows-only · Screen fixtures keep only signature rows — A screen fixture keeps only the rows holding a compiled signature literal, the rest blanked; a kept row the scrub would rewrite, or a username split across a row seam, refuses the recording.
+decision/screen-fixture-signature-rows-only · Screen fixtures keep only signature rows — A screen fixture keeps only signature rows (a row holding a compiled footer or modal literal whole, a box rule row as its rule chars alone, a prompt row as the prompt char alone), the rest blanked; another box row, a kept row the scrub would rewrite or a username split across a row seam is refused.
 decision/settings-override-plain-path · Settings override only for plain paths — The settings override is written only for a pinned path of plain characters. · why: a shell runs the override unquoted
@@ -422,5 +423,4 @@
 decision/cargo-deny-audit · cargo-deny as audit tool — cargo-deny 0.20.2 or newer audits advisories, bans, licences and sources.
-decision/cargo-deny-gate-clean · cargo-deny gate with no advisory ignores — CI's supply-chain gate runs cargo deny over advisories, bans, licenses and sources with the advisory ignore list empty.
 decision/checkout-no-persisted-credentials · Checkout without persisted credentials — The CI checkout action runs with persist-credentials false.
-decision/ci-cargo-deny-gate · cargo-deny gate in CI — CI runs cargo deny check over all four check families on the root lockfile and fails the build on any advisory, yanked crate or unknown source; the fuzz lockfile is audited for advisories and sources in its own step.
+decision/ci-cargo-deny-gate · cargo-deny gate in CI — CI runs cargo deny check over all four check families on the root lockfile and fails the build on any advisory not on its reasoned ignore list, any yanked crate or unknown source; the fuzz lockfile is audited for advisories and sources in its own step.
 decision/cli-tool-exact-pins · Exact pins for external CLI tools — External CLI and audit tools are installed at exact pinned versions, in CI and by the ripgrep install script, and CI actions are pinned by commit SHA; no tool is expressed as a minimum version floor. · why: CI installs each tool at its pin itself, and no drift check compares a locally installed build against a pin.
