 decision/no-c-building-crates · No C-building crates — Crates that build C code are banned in the root dependency graph by cargo-deny. · guard: scripts/deny-probes.sh
-decision/no-ignored-advisories · No ignored advisories — cargo-deny treats unmaintained and unsound advisories as failures, denies yanked crates and ignores no advisory; a new ignore follows the Critical CVE response SLA, its reason naming the disabled feature.
 decision/no-rust-cache-in-release · No rust-cache in the release workflow — Swatinem/rust-cache is never restored in the v1.x release workflow.
@@ -456,3 +455,5 @@
 decision/release-cache-poisoning-addressed · Cache-poisoning findings addressed before release — A v1.x release requires zizmor's cache-poisoning findings to be addressed.
+decision/rmcp-advisory-ignores · Reasoned advisory ignores for disabled rmcp features — cargo-deny treats unmaintained and unsound advisories as failures, denies yanked crates and ignores exactly RUSTSEC-2026-0457, RUSTSEC-2026-0461 and RUSTSEC-2026-0462, each in an rmcp feature banned or off in the release graph, its reason naming it, standing until rmcp leaves its below-3.5 range. · why: Ratified, under the Critical CVE response for an advisory confined to a disabled feature.
